First, we know there were **7 customers** in total. Out of these, **5 didn't leave a tip**. To find out how many customers did leave a tip, we subtract the number of customers who didn't tip from the total number of customers:

$$
7 \text{ (total customers)} - 5 \text{ (no tip)} = 2 \text{ (customers who tipped)}
$$

Each of these 2 customers left **$3**, so we multiply the number of tippers by the amount each gave:

$$
2 \text{ (customers)} \times \$3 \text{ (per customer)} = \$6
$$

The problem specifically asks how much money the waiter earned, and since it only mentions the tips from the customers, we can conclude that the total earnings from tips are **$6**.

