1. Calculate the total number of pieces for each type of candy separately.
   - Chocolate candy: $ 2 \text{ boxes} \times 4 \text{ pieces per box} $
   - Caramel candy: $ 5 \text{ boxes} \times 4 \text{ pieces per box} $
2. Add the two totals to get the overall amount of candy.

